# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ClimbIQ — environment variables
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to `.env.local`:   cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. Paste your Meta Model API key below (replace the placeholder).
#   3. Restart the dev server.
#
# IMPORTANT
#   - This key is read ONLY by the serverless function (netlify/functions/coach.ts
#     on Netlify, api/coach.ts on Vercel). It is never bundled into the frontend.
#     Do NOT prefix it with `VITE_` (anything starting with VITE_ is exposed to
#     the browser).
#   - `.env.local` is git-ignored. Never commit a real key.
#   - On Netlify, set this variable under:
#     Site settings → Environment variables (name: META_API_KEY), then redeploy.
#   - On Vercel, set it under Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Meta Model API key (get one at https://dev.meta.ai).
# ↓↓↓  PASTE YOUR KEY HERE  ↓↓↓
META_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides (sensible defaults are used if left unset).
# Base URL for the OpenAI-compatible Meta Model API.
META_API_BASE_URL=https://api.meta.ai/v1
# Model id used for coaching (multimodal reasoning model).
META_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3
